<title>USA: Sherwood Group Inc Q2 Nov 30 net firm.</title>
<headline>Sherwood Group Inc Q2 Nov 30 net firm.</headline>
<dateline>JERSEY CITY, N.J. 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996		1995</p>
<p>				(In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p> Revenues			    $   41,059	$   35,101</p>
<p> Operating income			 6,310	     4,141</p>
<p> Income before income taxes	   5,567	     3,672</p>
<p> Income taxes (b)			 2,272		 499</p>
<p> Net income				 3,295	     3,173</p>
<p> Net income per share		     .25		 .24</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding    13,028,509	13,425,900</p>
<p>						Six Months Ended</p>
<p> Revenues			    $   84,060	$   74,853</p>
<p> Operating income (a)		  12,355	    12,120</p>
<p> Income before income taxes	  11,587	    10,847</p>
<p> Income taxes (b)			 5,289	     3,206</p>
<p> Net income				 6,298	     7,641</p>
<p> Net income per share		     .48		 .57</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding    13,039,467	13,325,472</p>
<p>NOTES: (a) Declining operating income margin reflects an approximate 20 percent increase in staff size and the additional depreciation associated with the capital expenditures incurred in connection with the relocation of Sherwood Securities' and NDB's headquarters.</p>
<p>(b) The company's effective tax rate increased to about 41 percent in the latest quarter from 14 pct a year earlier and to 46 pct in the latest six mths from 30 pct for the six months ended November 30. The difference is due to several factors -- the company's relocation to New Jersey from New York during November 1995 led to a retroactive reduction in the company's effective tax rate during the quarter ended November 30, 1995. During the same quarter, the company recognized tax benefits related to employee compensation.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
